title    everything should be fast
date     2026-07-29
tags     speed optimisation rot
stage    budding
contra   on-slowness
---
A page that takes two seconds to load has already lost the argument. Weight is
a moral position: every kilobyte you ship is bandwidth someone else pays for,
on a phone, on a train, on a plan that meters it.

The whole of this site — parser, server, templates, stylesheet — is smaller
than one JavaScript framework's *runtime*. That is not a boast. That is the
baseline, and the industry has simply forgotten it.

> Measured, not asserted: `make check` fails the build if any page goes over
> budget. The machine holds the line, because I won't.

See also [[phyllotaxis]] — an SVG that weighs less than the photograph of the
thing it draws.
